# Trusted lines of the Isabelle-LLVM prototype (format: ../count-trusted.sh).
#
# Modelling style: trusted shim. Isabelle-LLVM has no function-pointer
# type and calls external functions by name only, so each indirect call
# is made by a C shim. In VU.thy the shim functions are constants with
# no definition and no axiom; the client's contract on each one is a
# hypothesis of the theorem that uses it, so the theorems hold for any
# shim and client that meet those hypotheses, and nothing else is
# assumed. A client function pointer is an opaque "8 word ptr".
#
# The shim: three C functions that make the indirect calls and return
# the callee's raw result; vu_call_apply_all also takes the address of
# the verified vu_i_apply (re-entrancy shape (a)).
shim.c
